    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d491">

                <pb facs="0859" n="727" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv01/pg727"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860c.01/6–2845: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 491<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy
                    </hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State ad interim</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caserta</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-06-28T12:00:00+02:00">June 28,
                            1945—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2795. Broad showed us a tel he has just
                        recd from ForOff instructing him if SAC<anchor n="1" xml:id="d491-f1"/> perceived no objection to
                    proceeding Polish GHQs in Italy and explain to Gen Anders in as favorable a manner as possible
                    why Poles abroad should welcome formation of new Pole Govt. ForOff was [<hi rendition="#italic">has</hi>]
                    authorized Broad to give to Anders story of Moscow negotiations more or
                    less as outlined in Depcirtels on this
                        subject<anchor n="2" xml:id="d491-f2"/> and to point out obvious advantages
                    accruing to Poland by constitution of new Govt. …</p>
                <p>Sent Dept, rptd
                    Moscow 188.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
